  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_11' aria-label=\" Tharammel Peethambaran and Another versus T. Ushakrishnan and Another pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('11','2026','2026_2_576_595','2026INSC134'); ><font size='4'> <strong>THARAMMEL PEETHAMBARAN AND ANOTHER<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>T. USHAKRISHNAN AND ANOTHER </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 2 S.C.R. 576</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 134</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010000562026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : PANKAJ MITHAL<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, SARASA VENKATANARAYANA BHATTI</strong><br> Issue for Consideration The controversy centres around the disputed circumstance, namely, the power of agency given by the plaintiff to the 1st Defendant through Exh.B-2. Whether the documentary evidence in Exh.B-2 satisfies the requirement of law and whether it is fudged with Procedure, 1908 &ndash; ss.100 and 103 &ndash; Evidence Act, 1872 &ndash; s.85 &ndash; Registration Act, 1908 &ndash; s.33 &ndash; On 31.07.1998, the plaintiff executed a Power of Attorney (PoA) in favour of the 1st defendant &ndash; The Plaintiff is the 1st Defendant&rsquo;s sister &ndash; The<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 06-02-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 856/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Dismissed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('11','2026','2026_2_576_595','2026INSC134','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split vie